      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Wan 2.1 VACE 1.3B - CHARACTER SWAP\n\nPuts **your character** (reference image) into a new scene.\n\n### How to use\n1. Put a picture of the character in `ComfyUI\\input\\` (any name, e.g. `character.png`).\n2. Click the image node and pick it.\n3. Describe the scene + what they do in the prompt.\n4. Press **Run**.\n\nThe result is a 3.4 s clip with that character's face, hair and clothes carried over.\n\n### Defaults\n- 704 x 480, 81 frames, **20 steps, CFG 6** (this model is not distilled)\n- About **1.5-2 min** per clip\n\n### Notes\n- Best with a clear, front-facing, well-lit reference photo.\n- Lower `strength` (0.7-0.9) if the face is copied too rigidly.\n- This is VACE reference-to-video. Wan 2.2 *Animate* gives better swaps but is a\n  14B model (~30 GB) and cannot run on 6 GB VRAM.\n\nModels used: Wan21-VACE-1.3B-Q8_0.gguf, umt5-xxl-encoder-Q4_K_M.gguf, wan_2.1_vae.safetensors"
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
